body:
PRD DRAFT 1 REVIEW — ACK THE SPINE AFTER FOUR BLOCKING AMENDMENTS. These are not vocabulary objections; each closes a false proof the current draft could still publish.

1. SECTION C STILL DROPS PLAN ADMISSION BETWEEN GEOMETRY AND RESOLUTION

R2 correctly says geometry is not admissibility, but C then jumps from C2 geometry to C3 per-family resolution/joint compatibility. R4(c) refers to an “unlawful” global plan without publishing the task/grain/eligible-region law that makes it unlawful.

Do not freeze “four coordinates” as the number. Publish at least these separate predicates:

- structural graph validity;
- observation/task identity: transcript, eligible-region mask, construction grain, coordinate dialect;
- derived geometry: order, overlap, cells, gaps, coverage, lengths;
- plan admission: the geometry satisfies the named task/grain/gap/minimum-cell policy;
- per-family outcomes plus joint plan/interpretation compatibility;
- construction route/provenance, calibration, adjudication, and use-specific scientific admission.

This resolves Q-C: CELL LENGTH is derived geometry; MINIMUM PERMITTED CELL LENGTH is a task/grain-specific admission rule. Eligibility says what text the plan is obliged to account for; it is not the minimum-cell rule itself.

The R2 positive court also needs an objective oracle, not “a human can see.” Freeze two explicit different cell sequences over the same synthetic/admitted transcript, eligible mask, grain, and policy; both must pass the same named plan law. Their differing exact boundaries are the executable fact.

2. R3.4 PROVES INTEGRITY, NOT AUTHENTICITY

Recomputing every binding from retained bytes can prove that content, ledgers, policy, and receipt are internally consistent. It cannot prove that a caller-written provider identity or adjudication receipt was genuinely issued. A caller can forge a self-consistent ledger and recompute an ordinary checksum.

The PRD must state the trust model:

- deterministic resolver decisions are replayed from bytes;
- provider/adjudicator authority is verified against an admitted registry, keyed authority, signature, or equivalent trust root when the scientific use requires authenticity;
- absent that root, decoding yields self-consistent-but-unverified provenance and cannot mint the corresponding scientific admission witness.

embed-core already distinguishes plain content integrity from keyed authority and reconstructs provider results under a trusted batch snapshot. That is the relevant pattern. Add an R3 court for FORGED BUT INTERNALLY CONSISTENT BYTES; mutation-only and no-upgrade round trips do not exercise it.

3. Q-A MUST BE A SET-LEVEL OBSERVATION MODEL

The draft still writes p(proposal at g | latent gap h), singular. One provider call normally emits a SET of gaps for one transcript. A pointwise product lets an over-segmenting provider manufacture arbitrary support by emitting 412, 413, 414, 415 around one latent boundary, even if calls/providers are correctly deduplicated.

Q-A must model the full emitted set conditional on a latent exact plan, or use an equivalent assignment/detection model that receipts:

- unmatched emitted gaps as false positives;
- unmatched latent gaps as misses;
- location error;
- at most one match contribution per observed and latent gap;
- proposal-count/over-segmentation tendency;
- provider-family and repeated-call dependence;
- one call receipt binding the proposal set.

Add the measured permutation failure to M0 explicitly: equal-evidence 412/413 resolves to 412 forward and 413 reversed on current main. R4 court 5 is therefore a red regression fact, not only a future requirement.

Add set-level courts: dense-provider invariance, one-to-many refusal, two-nearby-real-boundaries control, and call-group identity. A pointwise kernel may remain a component only inside this normalized set model.

4. R8 “ROBUSTNESS RANGE” NEEDS SUPPORT COMPLETENESS

For an uncalibrated partial family, min/max over the K constructions inspected is an observed sensitivity envelope, not a robustness range over admissible constructions. An omitted construction may lie outside it. “Robust” is licensed only when:

- the admissible construction universe is complete; or
- a sound search/bound proves no omitted construction violates the range.

Otherwise publish the enumerated family, exact support-selection receipt, and observed envelope with an explicit non-exhaustive label. Later calibrated truncation still needs captured/tail mass as already stated.

WITH THESE AMENDMENTS

I support the PRD’s core: R1 independent hygiene; structural-only bare decode; multi-coordinate authority; exact-gap/region/global-plan boundary resolution; invariant-breach exception retained; 2x2 compatibility; unweighted complete-artifact sensitivity first; estimand-specific courts; identity/crosswalk separation; immediate safety labels; parallel EventRecall plus gold tracks; and no lattice/SOTA claim before empirical value.

I would mark Q-A more precisely as “set-valued provider observation model over exact global plans,” add explicit ownership of the plan-admission policy, and leave R1/R10 merely READY PENDING CHIEF AUTHORITY — this proposal itself cannot make them buildable.

No implementation, public vocabulary, ADR, bead, dependency, path, reservation, data import, or authority claimed.
